Trio or from G7SensorKit.

THIRD-PARTY NOTICE — :wear, direct-to-watch
===========================================

The watch side of direct-to-watch (package app.aaps.wear.watchdirect) follows
the behaviour of nightscout/AndroidAPS pull request 5397, "Dexcom G7 direct"
(author t1dude / Magnus), at commit bec1b16ba20:

  - wear/src/main/kotlin/app/aaps/wear/g7/G7WatchReadings.kt
      -> WatchDirectReadings.kt (closely ported: the same rules for which
         reading the face shows, the graph merge, the delta, and when the
         watch raises its own low alarm)
  - wear/src/main/kotlin/app/aaps/wear/g7/G7WatchDirect.kt
  - wear/src/main/kotlin/app/aaps/wear/g7/G7WatchService.kt
  - wear/src/main/kotlin/app/aaps/wear/g7/G7WatchActivity.kt
      -> WatchDirect.kt, WatchDirectService.kt, WatchDirectActivity.kt
         (re-built on this repository's own Dexcom ONE+ / G7 driver,
         :plugins:dexcom_oneplus, through WatchSensorLink; the structure and
         some text follow the originals)

The phone side (plugins/source, DexcomOnePlusWatchDirectRules and
DexcomOnePlusWatchHandover) follows
cgm/dexcomg7/src/main/kotlin/app/aaps/cgm/dexcomg7/watch/G7WatchHandover.kt of
the same pull request and commit.

No sensor protocol code was taken from that pull request. The sensor protocol
used on the watch is this repository's own driver and the vendored xDrip keks
library (:plugins:libkeks, GPL-3.0, see plugins/libkeks/NOTICE). The protocol
code of pull request 5397 is itself a port of Trio's G7SensorKit
